{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["No straw is given — with a qamatz: 'it is not given to us,' but it was given to us previously. נִתַּן הַכְּסִיל (Ecclesiastes 10)." "And the sin of your people — if it has a dagesh and a qamatz, this is how it must be explained: 'We are beaten, and here your people are committing a sin with you.' But if it were חֲטָאת with a pataḥ, its meaning would be 'the sin-offering of your people.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The lemma reads חַטָּאת (dagesh + qamatz); Rashbam contrasts it with a hypothetical חֲטָאת (pataḥ). The English 'sin-offering' is used solely to reflect the traditional reading the hypothetical form would evoke, not to render a divine name."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:30.021521813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}